  "diagnostics": {
    "selection": [
      {
        "bio": "S001213",
        "speaker": "Bryan Steil",
        "side": "Yea",
        "manager": true,
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-22/html/CREC-2026-07-22-pt1-PgH5143.htm",
        "start": 17939,
        "quote": "Mr. Speaker, I rise today in support of the Stop Insider Trading Act. \nThere is a lot of talk in this town about draining the swamp and \ncleaning up Washington. Today, the rubber hits the road. Good \ngovernance matters, and the Committee on House Administration is \nleading the way.",
        "summary": "I rise today in support of the Stop Insider Trading Act.",
        "index": 0,
        "reason": "Directly supports the bill."
      },
      {
        "bio": "S001213",
        "speaker": "Bryan Steil",
        "side": "Yea",
        "manager": true,
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-22/html/CREC-2026-07-22-pt1-PgH5143.htm",
        "start": 18224,
        "quote": "Under current law, Members of Congress are required to publicly \ndisclose their stock trades. The disclosures lack details and are often \nfiled months after a transaction.",
        "summary": "Under current law, Members of Congress are required to publicly disclose their stock trades. The disclosures lack details and are often filed months after a transaction.",
        "index": 8,
        "reason": "Identifies a transparency gap the bill addresses."
      },
      {
        "bio": "K000398",
        "speaker": "Thomas H. Kean, Jr.",
        "side": "Yea",
        "manager": false,
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-22/html/CREC-2026-07-22-pt1-PgH5143.htm",
        "start": 56330,
        "quote": "That is why I strongly support the Stop Insider Trading Act, which \nwould prohibit Members of Congress, their spouses, and dependent \nchildren from purchasing individual stocks.",
        "summary": "That is why I strongly support the Stop Insider Trading Act, which would prohibit Members of Congress, their spouses, and dependent children from purchasing individual stocks.",
        "index": 13,
        "reason": "States support for the core prohibition in the bill."
      },
      {
        "bio": "S001213",
        "speaker": "Bryan Steil",
        "side": "Yea",
        "manager": true,
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-22/html/CREC-2026-07-22-pt1-PgH5143.htm",
        "start": 18398,
        "quote": "This lack of transparency and the continued practice of Members \npurchasing stock is fueling public frustration. It is time we ban \nMembers of Congress from being able to buy individual companies' shares \nof stock. Doing so removes even the appearance of impropriety.",
        "summary": "This lack of transparency and the continued practice of Members purchasing stock is fueling public frustration. It is time we ban Members of Congress from being able to buy individual companies' shares of stock. Doing so removes even the appearance of impropriety.",
        "index": 16,
        "reason": "Gives a substantive justification for banning congressional stock purchases."
      },
      {
        "bio": "S001213",
        "speaker": "Bryan Steil",
        "side": "Yea",
        "manager": true,
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-22/html/CREC-2026-07-22-pt1-PgH5143.htm",
        "start": 18668,
        "quote": "Mr. Speaker, we have an opportunity to pass transformational \ncongressional ethics reform. This is the first congressional stock \ntrading ban to receive a vote on the floor of the House. Today, every \nAmerican will know where their Member stands.",
        "summary": "We have an opportunity to pass transformational congressional ethics reform. This is the first congressional stock trading ban to receive a vote on the floor of the House. Today, every American will know where their Member stands.",
        "index": 24,
        "reason": "Supports the reform as a meaningful ethics measure."
      },
      {
        "bio": "S001213",
        "speaker": "Bryan Steil",
        "side": "Yea",
        "manager": true,
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-22/html/CREC-2026-07-22-pt1-PgH5143.htm",
        "start": 18917,
        "quote": "If you want to day trade, there is a place for that. It is called \nWall Street. If you want to come to Washington, you should be working \non behalf of the American people.",
        "summary": "If you want to day trade, there is a place for that. It is called Wall Street. If you want to come to Washington, you should be working on behalf of the American people.",
        "index": 31,
        "reason": "Explains why Members should not trade stocks while serving."
      },
      {
        "bio": "M001206",
        "speaker": "Joseph D. Morelle",
        "side": "Nay",
        "manager": true,
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-22/html/CREC-2026-07-22-pt1-PgH5143.htm",
        "start": 20521,
        "quote": "Mr. Speaker, what we are considering here today is a remarkable \ndisplay of cynicism, even for this institution, even for this \nRepublican leadership team.",
        "summary": "what we are considering here today is a remarkable display of cynicism, even for this institution, even for this Republican leadership team.",
        "index": 0,
        "reason": "Frames the bill as cynical rather than a genuine reform."
      },
      {
        "bio": "M001206",
        "speaker": "Joseph D. Morelle",
        "side": "Nay",
        "manager": true,
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-22/html/CREC-2026-07-22-pt1-PgH5143.htm",
        "start": 21188,
        "quote": "What are Speaker Johnson and House Republicans doing about this? They \nare pretending here on the floor today to address the issue. They are \npushing the so-called Stop Insider Trading Act, a name meant entirely \nto trick the American people.",
        "summary": "they are pretending here on the floor today to address the issue.",
        "index": 14,
        "reason": "Argues the measure is only a pretense, not a real attempt to solve the problem."
      },
      {
        "bio": "M001206",
        "speaker": "Joseph D. Morelle",
        "side": "Nay",
        "manager": true,
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-22/html/CREC-2026-07-22-pt1-PgH5143.htm",
        "start": 21433,
        "quote": "This bill, quite simply, is a sham. The bill allows Members of the \nCongress to continue owning and trading stocks. That is right. The so-\ncalled Stop Insider Trading Act actually allows Members of Congress to \nown and trade stocks.",
        "summary": "This bill, quite simply, is a sham.",
        "index": 21,
        "reason": "Directly characterizes the bill as illegitimate and deceptive."
      },
      {
        "bio": "M001206",
        "speaker": "Joseph D. Morelle",
        "side": "Nay",
        "manager": true,
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-22/html/CREC-2026-07-22-pt1-PgH5143.htm",
        "start": 21668,
        "quote": "Even this half measure--or should I say quarter measure--goes too far \nfor Republican leadership. How do we know? What is the tell? How do we \nknow that the Republican posturing is all performative and that \nRepublicans do not want a stock trading bill ban to become law? They \nhave added a poison pill to this bill. They have added provisions that \nhave absolutely nothing to do with stock trading and everything to do \nwith their obsession with the 2020 election.",
        "summary": "Even this half measure--or should I say quarter measure--goes too far for Republican leadership.",
        "index": 28,
        "reason": "Undercuts the bill as an inadequate compromise that still fails to reflect real opposition."
      },
      {
        "bio": "M001206",
        "speaker": "Joseph D. Morelle",
        "side": "Nay",
        "manager": true,
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-22/html/CREC-2026-07-22-pt1-PgH5143.htm",
        "start": 39087,
        "quote": "This will not fix anything, and that is what it is intended to do, to \nnot fix anything, but to make people believe that we have addressed it. \nWe haven't addressed anything.",
        "summary": "This will not fix anything, and that is what it is intended to do, to not fix anything, but to make people believe that we have addressed it.",
        "index": 52,
        "reason": "States the bill is designed to create the appearance of action without solving the issue."
      },
      {
        "bio": "M001206",
        "speaker": "Joseph D. Morelle",
        "side": "Nay",
        "manager": true,
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-22/html/CREC-2026-07-22-pt1-PgH5143.htm",
        "start": 47003,
        "quote": "Others have pointed out Democratic Members and recognized them. There \nare glaring examples here. However, to reiterate the point, this bill \nwould not prevent insider trading. It would just trick the American \npeople into thinking we are trying to do something about corruption \nwhen we are not.",
        "summary": "this bill would not prevent insider trading. It would just trick the American people into thinking we are trying to do something about corruption when we are not.",
        "index": 57,
        "reason": "Asserts the bill fails on its stated purpose and only misleads the public."
      }
